{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and the Rude Customer", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "De-Stress", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Food for Thought > Overeating", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and provide solutions to problems in a range of social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing What is Necessary", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modals like <span class=\"italic\">should</span> and <span class=\"italic\">must</span> or expressions like <span class=\"italic\">You have got to \u2026</span> or <span class=\"italic\">You are going to have to ...</span> to express what is necessary.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the following to express what is necessary:<br> <ul><li>You had better ... </li> <li>You have got to ... </li> <li>I'm going to have to ... </li><li>You must ...</li> <li>You need to ... </li><li>You should ... </li><li>You might want to  ... </li><li> You ought to ... </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Manager</span>: You should get more sleep.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Waiter</span>: You're right. I also ought to exercise more. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Manager</span>: You might want to join a BJJ class!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Remember that <span class=\"italic\">should</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might want to ... </span> imply milder necessity, while <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have got to ... </span> and <span class=\"italic\">had better ... </span> imply stronger necessity.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbs of Manner", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use adverbs of manner to describe how something is done. They give more specific information about the verb. <Br> <span class=\"italic\">Example: She walked slowly.<br> How did she walk? Slowly.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Many adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ly</span> to adjective:<br><span class=\"italic\"> Examples: sad - sadly, curious - curiously</span><br><br>   Some adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ily</span> to adjectives ending in -y:<br> <span class=\"italic\">Example: angry - angrily</span><br><br>  The adverbs <span class=\"strong\">fast</span>, <span class=\"strong\">hard</span>, <span class=\"strong\">well</span> and <span class=\"strong\">straight</span> are exceptions. They do not change when they become adverbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"light<br> well<br>\\t\\t\\t different<br>\\t\\t anxious\\t<br>\\t quiet\\t<br>\\t physical\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lightly<br> well<br> differently<br> anxiously<br> quietly<br> physically\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I followed your advice about taking things lightly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I started behaving differently.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You usually place adverbs of manner after the main verb, or after the direct object if there is one. The adverb cannot go in between the direct object and the verb. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Incorrect</span>:  <span class=\"italic\">She ate slowly the cookie.</span> <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Correct</span>: <span class=\"italic\">She ate the cookie slowly.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lightly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not seriously ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should take things lightly at work sometimes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about healthy habits at work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Brazilian jiujitsu", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a form of martial art derived from judo ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love Brazilian jiu jitsu. It helps me work better.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "focused ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "able to concentrate on a task ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: BJJ helps me stay focused at work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "work-life balance ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the importance you put on work compared to other things, like family and friends ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's important to keep a healthy  work-life balance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "differently ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in a different manner ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I started behaving differently. I'm less anxious now!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le05ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of a stressful situation in your life at work, school or home.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about your way to de-stress with